This agreement covers the Sapling library: the SAS macros (the files of this
folder, and the copy shipped in DataStep Studio for SAS) and the R package
"sapling", with their documentation, examples and tutorials ("the Library").
The Library is commercial software. It is licensed, not sold.


1. Definitions

   "You" is the company, institution or person that holds the license.
   "Licensed User" is a named person whom you allow to use the Library and for
   whom you hold a paid seat (a "Seat").
   "Study Programs" are the programs, data sets, tables, listings, figures and
   other results that a Licensed User makes with the Library.
   "Study Deliverables" are the Study Programs of one clinical study, or one
   project, as handed over to the persons named in section 4.


2. License grant

   While you hold a valid paid license, and for its number of Seats, each
   Licensed User may:
   (a) install and run the Library, on any computer and SAS or R server that
       you use;
   (b) read the source code, and change it for your own internal use; a
       changed copy stays under this agreement;
   (c) write Study Programs that call the Library, for your own studies and,
       as a contract research organization or a consultant, for the studies of
       your clients.

   Early Access: while DataStep Studio holds a valid Early Access entitlement,
   the Library may be used free of charge under the terms of this agreement.
   Early Access is temporary. After it ends, the Library requires a paid
   license.


3. Your results are yours

   The Study Programs and their results belong to you (or to your client), not
   to DataStep Labs. DataStep Labs claims no rights in your data, your programs
   or your results.


4. Study deliverables and regulatory submissions

   You may include copies of the parts of the Library that your Study Programs
   call (changed or unchanged) in the Study Deliverables that you give to:
   (a) the sponsor of the study, and your client;
   (b) regulatory authorities, such as the FDA, EMA, PMDA and national
       authorities, in a submission or on their request;
   (c) auditors, inspectors, reviewers, ethics committees and data monitoring
       committees of the study;
   (d) a future owner of the study, if the study is sold or transferred.

   These recipients need no license and pay no fee. They may use these copies
   only to read, run again, check and review the Study Programs of that study,
   and to keep them in the archive of that study. They may not use the copies
   for other studies or projects, unless they hold their own license. Keep this
   license notice with the copies.


5. Archived studies

   When your license ends, you may keep the copies of the Library that are in
   the archives of studies made while the license was valid, and run them
   again to reproduce, check or defend the results of those studies. You may
   not use them to write new Study Programs or for new studies.


6. Restrictions

   You may not:
   (a) give, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or publish the Library, or a changed
       copy, except as section 4 allows;
   (b) let persons who are not Licensed Users use the Library, except as
       sections 4 and 5 allow;
   (c) use more Seats than you paid for, or share one Seat between persons;
   (d) use the Library, or a changed copy of it, to make or offer a product or
       a macro library that competes with the Library;
   (e) remove or change the copyright notices, the license notices or the
       headers of the files;
   (f) get around the license check of DataStep Studio.


7. Fees

   The fees, the term of the license and the number of Seats are those of your
   order or subscription. A subscription renews for its term unless it is
   cancelled before the end of its term.


8. No warranty

   THE LIBRARY IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

   You are responsible for the validation of the Library in your environment
   and for checking the results of your Study Programs, as the regulations
   and your own procedures require.


9. Limitation of liability

   TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, DATASTEP LABS SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY
   INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE USE
   OF THE LIBRARY. THE TOTAL LIABILITY OF DATASTEP LABS IS LIMITED TO THE FEES
   YOU PAID FOR THE LIBRARY IN THE TWELVE MONTHS BEFORE THE CLAIM.


10. Termination

   This license ends at the end of its term, or when you breach it and do not
   cure the breach within 30 days of a notice. When it ends, stop using the
   Library, except as sections 4 and 5 allow.


11. Trademarks

